SUMMARY:🍽️ Dinner: Spicy Sriracha Noodles
DESCRIPTION:Recipe: Spicy Sriracha Noodles\nServings: 2\nPrep: 5 min | Cook: 10 min | Total: 15 min\n\n--- Ingredients ---\n• 4.0 oz lo mein noodles\n• 2.0 tbsp vegan butter (Earth Balance)\n• 0.25 tsp crushed red pepper\n• 2.0 large eggs\n• 1.0 tbsp brown sugar\n• 1.0 tbsp soy sauce\n• 2.0 tbsp sriracha\n• 1.0 handful fresh cilantro\n• 1.0 green onion, sliced\n\n--- Steps ---\n1. Prepare the sauce for the noodles. In a small bowl, stir together the brown sugar, soy sauce, and sriracha. Set the sauce aside.\n2. Bring a pot of water to a boil for the noodles. Once boiling, add the noodles and boil until tender. Drain the noodles in a colander.\n3. While waiting for the water to boil, crack two eggs into a bowl then whisk lightly.\n4. Heat the butter in a skillet over medium heat, then add the eggs and crushed pepper and lightly scramble the eggs. Avoid over cooking the eggs.\n5. Once the noodles have drained, add them to the skillet with the eggs, then drizzle the sauce over top. Toss the noodles and eggs to coat in the sauce.\n6. Top the noodles with fresh cilantro and sliced green onion, then serve.\n\nTip: 🥛 DAIRY-FREE SWAPS: butter → vegan butter (Earth Balance). These sweet, tangy, and spicy sriracha noodles take only a few minutes to make and are an inexpensive alternative to take out.\n\nSource: https://www.budgetbytes.com/dragon-noodles/
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://www.budgetbytes.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/08/Spicy-Noodles-skillet.jpg
URL:https://www.budgetbytes.com/dragon-noodles/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mealplan-20260610-breakfast-112@mealplanner
DTSTAMP:20260430T211848Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T090000
SUMMARY:🍳 Breakfast: Savory Oatmeal
DESCRIPTION:Recipe: Savory Oatmeal\nServings: 1\nPrep: 5 min | Cook: 10 min | Total: 15 min\n\n--- Ingredients ---\n• 1.0 clove garlic, minced\n• 0.5 tsp grated fresh ginger\n• 4.0 mushrooms\n• 1.0 tsp vegan butter (Earth Balance)\n• 1.0 cup vegetable broth\n• 0.5 cup old-fashioned rolled oats\n• 0.5 cup spinach\n• 0.5 tsp toasted sesame oil\n\n--- Steps ---\n1. Mince the garlic, grate the ginger, and slice the mushrooms.\n2. Add the butter, garlic, and ginger to a small saucepot. Sauté over medium heat for 1-2 minutes.\n3. Add the mushrooms and continue to sauté for a few minutes more, or until the mushrooms have wilted a bit.\n4. Add the vegetable broth to the saucepot, turn the heat up to medium-high, and bring the broth up to a boil.\n5. When the broth reaches a boil, add the rolled oats and stir to combine. Allow it to return to a boil, then reduce the heat to medium low. Let the oats simmer for about 5 minutes, or until thickened.\n6. While the oats are simmering, roughly chop the spinach. Stir the spinach into the thickened oats, along with the toasted sesame oil.\n7. Taste and add salt to your liking, if needed, then top it off with your favorite toppings. Serve hot!\n\nTip: 🥛 DAIRY-FREE SWAPS: butter → vegan butter (Earth Balance). Savory oatmeal is a delicious, hearty, and inexpensive meal that can be customized to use ingredients you have on hand.\n\nSource: https://www.budgetbytes.com/savory-oatmeal/
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://www.budgetbytes.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Savory-Oatmeal-above.jpg
URL:https://www.budgetbytes.com/savory-oatmeal/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mealplan-20260610-lunch-113@mealplanner
DTSTAMP:20260430T211848Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T120000
